# Architectural debt that `deslop-please --allow .deslop-please.allow` still
# tolerates, run from `mqttiumd/` (deslop-please 0.1.3). Recorded on 23
# November 2026 at 290db2b, 87 entries; each lot of branch
# `refactor/deslop-layers` removes the entries it fixes. An entry still here is
# not fixed.
#
# Kept on purpose, with their reason:
# - long-file, wide-directory: splitting the long files re-points about 125
#   citations of conformance/server-statements.json and the replays of the
#   models, which CI checks; the structural lots change which files are long.
#   Decided after them.
# - shallow-module mqttiumd_store_api: `DurableStore` is the port every store
#   implements (eleven implementations); a trait that is the interface shows
#   its methods. Removing one method does not make it deep.
# - shallow-module mqttiumd_contract: a contract crate shows its types. Moving
#   the generic maps out (a crate of their own) reverses record 0057 and is a
#   separate proposal.
#
# The other entries are fixed lot by lot.
module-cycle mqttiumd::codec,mqttiumd::net,mqttiumd::security
module-cycle mqttiumd_contract::command,mqttiumd_contract::message_expiry,mqttiumd_contract::outcome,mqttiumd_contract::packet,mqttiumd_contract::properties,mqttiumd_contract::pubsub,mqttiumd_contract::retained,mqttiumd_contract::session,mqttiumd_contract::will
